findings.fix:
Replace the Node‑style `process.env` access with Vite's `import.meta.env` (or the appropriate bundler env accessor) and remove the unnecessary quote‑escaping. For example:
```tsx
// Replace this line
const baseUrl = (process.env.OMNIBRIDGE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL ?? "https://omnibridge-dev.vercel.app/api/v1").replace(/"/g, "\\\"");
// With something like this (assuming the env variable is prefixed with VITE_ as required by Vite)
const baseUrl = (import.meta.env.VITE_OMNIBRIDGE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL ?? "https://omnibridge-dev.vercel.app/api/v1");
```
Then keep the script injection unchanged:
```tsx
<script
  dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{
    __html: `window.__OMNIBRIDGE_BASE_URL__ = ${JSON.stringify(baseUrl)};`,
  }}
/>
```
